3h1d|v|To devour. ; To rub; to wear away by friction; to chafe; to gall; hence, to eat away; to gnaw; as, to fret cloth; to fret a piece of gold or other metal; a worm frets the plants of a ship. ; To impair; to wear away; to diminish. ; To make rough, agitate, or disturb; to cause to ripple; as, to fret the surface of water. ; To tease; to irritate; to vex. ; To be worn away; to chafe; to fray; as, a wristband frets on the edges. ; To eat in; to make way by corrosion. ; To be agitated; to be in violent commotion; to rankle; as, rancor frets in the malignant breast. ; To be vexed; to be chafed or irritated; to be angry; to utter peevish expressions. ; To ornament with raised work; to variegate; to diversify. ; To furnish with frets, as an instrument of music.	o:16og,75,20;s22,65,2;1hne,45,9;10d5,38,42;6dm9,37,1;6f7u,31,26;2ngr,28,1;5knm,26,3;2epi,19,2;2w6y,13,6;5kmj,11,2;8ru9,9,1;8w7x,9,1;3aqo,6,1;ah8m,6,1~10d5,38,42;6f7u,31,26;16og,75,20;1hne,45,9;954k,6,8;2w6y,13,6;5ltk,4,4;5knm,26,3;s22,65,2;5kmj,11,2;2epi,19,2;2ngr,28,1;ah8m,6,1;6dm9,37,1;8ru9,9,1	s:9x4x,77,5;19ou,66,2;s22,55,1;9hs9,49,3;3wjj,47,13;3917,37,6;8lbp,17,2~3wjj,47,13;3917,37,6;9x4x,77,5;9hs9,49,3;19ou,66,2;8lbp,17,2;s22,55,1	d:1k00,68,20~1k00,68,20	D:9qej,36,283~9qej,36,283
